          "page": 1,
          "section": "Abstract",
          "quote": "FCC-based high entropy alloys (HEAs) with exceptional cryogenic mechanical properties have the potential for use in strategic applications. In this regard, we have studied via transmission electron microscopy (TEM) the microstructural evolution of hierarchical nanotwins in tensile-strained Fe27Co24Ni23Cr26 HEA alloys as a function of true strain at cryogenic temperature and compared the behavior at room temperature.",
